# Copilot Instructions: Fitness Tracker

## Architecture
- Use modular, maintainable code (separate routes, models, controllers)
- Use environment variables for config and secrets
- Use async/await for all async code
- Use Mongoose for MongoDB models and validation

## Cross-Domain
- Ensure CORS is configured via environment variable
- API must validate and sanitize all input
- No secrets or credentials in code or logs

## Innovation
- Prioritize accessibility (ARIA, skip links, color contrast)
- Optimize for Lighthouse (performance, SEO, best practices)
- Use semantic HTML and meta tags
- Add tests for all new features

## Documentation
- Update README, SECURITY.md, DEPLOYMENT.md, DATABASE_SETUP.md for all major changes
- Document all API endpoints and environment variables
- Add code comments for complex logic

## General
- Use Helmet, compression, and CORS middleware
- Use graceful shutdown and health check endpoint
- Keep dependencies up to date
- Use .gitignore to exclude node_modules, .env, logs, build, and sensitive files
- Write clear, descriptive commit messages

